  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed additional storey, intended to provide residential accommodation, by reason of its scale, bulk, massing, and design, would constitute an overly dominant and discordant addition to the host property. It would fail to integrate with its surroundings and would be out of keeping with the established character of the area, causing harm to its visual appearance. These adverse impacts would not be outweighed by the limited public benefit of delivering additional residential units. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies DMD13 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document, CP30 and CP31 of the Core Strategy, Policies D4 and D5 of the London Plan (2021), and the aims and objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024)"
  ],
